{"run": "digest", "t": 56710, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [International relations] 2026 Bishkek SCO summit — The 26th Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) summit is held in Bishkek, Kyrgyzstan, which coincides with the country's Independence Day and the opening ceremony of the 2026 World Nomad Games."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 56710, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Armed conflicts and attacks] 2026 Iran war — The Washington Post reports that military leaders have warned U.S. Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth against prolonging the war in Iran to 2027."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 56710, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Armed conflicts and attacks] Sudanese civil war — Sudan's doctors network reports that five civilians have been killed and thousands have been displaced during attacks by Rapid Support Forces in Bara, North Kordofan."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 56710, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Armed conflicts and attacks] 2026 Nigerien coup attempt — Niger's army says that they have regained control of a airbase after it was attacked by mutiny soldiers yesterday."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 56710, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Disasters and accidents] 2026 Indonesia wildfires — A orangutan named Sampurna is reported to be rescued from a haze fire zone in Ketapang, West Kalimantan on Indonesia's Borneo island."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 56710, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Disasters and accidents] 2026 Indonesia wildfires — The Japan Maritime Self-Defense Force ship JS Kunisaki departs from a port in Kure, Japan to help fight forest fires in Indonesia."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 56710, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Disasters and accidents] Sinking of the Filo Jet — A passenger ferry, sailing from Cyprus to Turkey, capsizes in the eastern Mediterranean sea. The ship was carrying 259 passengers and 8 crew members, of which 237 people have been rescued."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 56710, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Disasters and accidents] The body of the last missing individual aboard a boat capsized on Thursday on Mapanuepe Lake in San Marcelino, Zambales, Philippines, is recovered, concluding search operations with the final death toll at nine."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 56710, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [International relations] 2026 state visit by Xi Jinping to Kyrgyzstan and Egypt — Chinese President Xi Jinping and his wife Peng Liyuan arrive at Manas International Airport in Kyrgyzstan for the upcoming Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) summit in Bishkek and a state visit to the country."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 56710, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Law and crime] One person is killed and five others are injured in a mass shooting at a rave in Aarau, Aargau, Switzerland. The perpetrator is on the run."}
